{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git status --short --branch; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git log -3 --oneline; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --format=fuller --stat b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --format= b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3; for f in AGENTS.md ../AGENTS.md ../../AGENTS.md; do if test -f \"$f\"; then cat \"$f\"; fi; done'","aggregated_output":"## HEAD (no branch)\n88630634 p1b-ci-r2: remove dead FFI helpers and classify native GC in JS audit\nf1a5c9f3 p1b-ci: guard emitted FFI heads and record per-install toolchain provenance\n3ecd20cc p1b-linux-r3: select and verify the platform errno accessor\ncommit b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Sat Oct 24 13:55:46 2026 +0700\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Sat Oct 24 13:55:46 2026 +0700\n\n    Refuse assoc on a deftype that is not Associative\n    \n    jolt-assoc1's jrec arm gave every jrec defrecord semantics, so\n    (assoc (T. 1) :b 2) on a plain deftype answered a fresh T while\n    (associative? (T. 1)) is false. On the JVM it throws ClassCastException.\n    The field/extension-map arm now applies to records only (jrec-record?);\n    a deftype declaring assoc still answers through it, and any other deftype\n    reaches the existing ClassCastException naming its class.\n\n host/chez/records-coll.ss | 6 +++++-\n 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/host/chez/records-coll.ss b/host/chez/records-coll.ss\nindex c65b1921..ad58ee6a 100644\n--- a/host/chez/records-coll.ss\n+++ b/host/chez/records-coll.ss\n@@ -476,10 +476,14 @@\n          (%r-jolt-nth coll i d)))))\n ;; assoc: replacing a declared field copies the value vector; any other key grows\n ;; the extension map (the value vector is shared — fields are immutable).\n+;; Only a defrecord is associative this way (IRecord, as on the JVM). A deftype\n+;; that declares assoc answers through it; any other deftype is not\n+;; Associative, so it falls through to the base refusal (ClassCastException,\n+;; naming the class), matching both the JVM and jolt's own associative?.\n (define %r-jolt-assoc1 jolt-assoc1)\n (set! jolt-assoc1 (lambda (coll k v)\n   (cond ((jrec-cl coll \"assoc\") => (lambda (m) (jolt-invoke m coll k v)))\n-        ((jrec? coll)\n+        ((jrec-record? coll)\n          (let ((i (and (keyword? k) (jrec-field-index coll k))))\n             (if i\n                 (let ((v2 (let ((flags (hashtable-ref chez-record-dbl-tbl (jrec-tag coll) #f)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
